{"id": "EUVD-2026-76677", "enisaUuid": "f9a1748a-4f70-3ba4-b3fb-0eb4f0d906e5", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ntimers/itimer: Zero-init old itimerval before copy to userspace\n\nOn native sparc64, struct __kernel_old_timeval contains a four-byte hole\nafter tv_usec because tv_sec is 64-bit while __kernel_suseconds_t is 32-bit.\nput_itimerval() fills only the named fields in a stack-allocated\n__kernel_old_itimerval and copies the entire object to userspace, so\ngetitimer() can expose the two padding holes.\n\nZero-initialize the aggregate before assigning the fields so implicit\npadding is deterministic before it crosses the user/kernel boundary.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:47:05", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:52:18", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6d4b937251386d9c6f968e7802f0cb16a8523772", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4ea70146ab9376092297eb8b622ef1792797f2cf", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a17b345daff46fec4af9f1ecbdf350208016dd15", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bdfda99c5763822a9a888e8af0ad7d9312ffcfe2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4c66719dd1e4023c5e3f7d050f1bbefec3dfbeb4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2bf5e8f7c9bf4ad3be343a9a6e3e50a34264d25e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/00ef529a5402f41eb1d227916437e237450719f9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/18c7d85864e554adc8fad1e8d2e9d2cb6c3911c8"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89765", "GHSA-x38g-mr96-v378"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0f7b7dec-2218-3761-be44-d78991ff65ee", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "13a8a4a7-5522-35b7-afa0-2a67b9a523f5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <4c66719dd1e4023c5e3f7d050f1bbefec3dfbeb4"}, {"id": "2631dfb3-777d-3058-8b67-86fc73c3af91", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}},